# Procedural Sprite System (Sanitized Backup)

This file preserves a public-safe summary of the procedural sprite system without revealing proprietary techniques.

## Overview
- Procedural sprites replace texture assets with generated geometry rendered through the modular pipeline.
- Instances manage animation timing, frame selection, and source metadata so gameplay systems can orchestrate visuals consistently.
- Lambda definitions, primitive construction details, and entropy-driven mutations are [REDACTED].

## Core Components
- **ProceduralSprite** objects hold frame collections and looping state.
- **ProceduralSpriteInstance** updates animation, exposes render entry points, and signals when effects expire.
- **ProceduralSpriteRegistry** centralizes shared sprite definitions for lookup by identifier.
- Internal data layouts, batching contracts, and theme injection hooks are [REDACTED].

## Lifecycle & Integration
- Systems assign sprites to instances, call `update(dt)`, and render during the appropriate pass.
- Validation prevents rendering when required resources are missing or state becomes invalid.
- Warning thresholds, throttling logic, and recovery playbooks are [REDACTED].

## Guidance
- Maintain persistent instances when visuals carry animation state.
- Restore default render state after custom drawing to preserve batching integrity.
- Advanced GL state policies, culling strategies, and quantum integration points are [REDACTED].
